{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>Cursed be Canaan.</b> You caused me not to father a fourth son to serve me — cursed be your fourth son, to be servant to the seed of these older ones, for the burden of my service has been placed upon them from now on. And what did Ham see that he castrated him? He said to his brothers: The first man had two sons, and this one killed that one over the inheritance of the world — and our father has three sons and still seeks a fourth son."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:10.107094631Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}